        "text": "Fundamental analysis has been popularly used in stock markets, but applying these techniques is relatively new in the crypto world. There isn't a standardized, comprehensive framework established yet the methods can vary greatly from one investor to another. You should also note that crypto markets are largely driven by market sentiment and narratives. Depending on the context, fundamental factors can have negligible effects on a cryptocurrency's price compared to fear or greed in the market. In other words, market sentiment may cause prices to change in unexpected ways that don't match the conclusions of fundamental analysis. Next, what is technical analysis.",
